  bootwright / explain
      Explain the stop codes apply and destroy report. With no flag it lists every stop; with
      --code it prints that stop's meaning, the level it stops at, whether its effect is
      certain, its cause, its recovery, whether repeating the command helps and its remedy. It
      reads no context and contacts nothing.

  Usage
    bootwright explain [flags]

  Command flags
      --code  Select one stop by its code

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  Examples
    bootwright explain --code runner.deadline
